{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1334553-how-claimed-leverage-their-influences","id":1334553,"title":"How claimed leverage their influences","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Werewolf: The Forsaken"],"posts":[{"date":"2019-09-08T16:43:24-07:00","id":1334553,"title":"How claimed leverage their influences","content":"This is regarding some of the cool inspirations that where in Shunned by the Moon, which was a great book for ideas.<br /> <br /> Regarding Broken Mirror, if she is fettered to her host, or possessing her, how does she use her influences? The book indicates that she can pass herself off as a friend of a pack to help them lower their rage (her influence is rage 2). The book seems to indicate that spirits cannot use influences when fettered or possessed, only claimed. If the spirit wanted to calm the rage of a pack, or incite them to rage, does the spirit need to temporarily eject from the host or just claim it if possible? In other words, how does a fettered spirit affect anything outside the host with influences?<br /> <br /> Another question regarding the claimed Alex Cecil, is the spirit focusing its influence on the host making him more desireable? or influencing everyone around him to increase their desire for him? Mind you, the influence of desire can also be mixed with the Numina of Emotional Implant to create a very good combo. <br /> <br /> Just curious because these are excellent examples of low level spirits doing really far reaching things in hosts and being able to leverage influences to become pretty powerful. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1107-maryshelly","name":"maryshelly","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1107_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"337"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-08T19:08:06-07:00","id":1334566,"title":"","content":"AFAIK, spirits lost access to numina if they were ridding someone. Not influences. Otherwise they wouldn't be able to manifest.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12191-malus","name":"Malus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12191_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1562"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-09T13:17:55-07:00","id":1334709,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>maryshelly</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1334553-how-claimed-leverage-their-influences#post1334553\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Regarding Broken Mirror, if she is fettered to her host, or possessing her, how does she use her influences? The book indicates that she can pass herself off as a friend of a pack to help them lower their rage (her influence is rage 2). The book seems to indicate that spirits cannot use influences when fettered or possessed, only claimed. If the spirit wanted to calm the rage of a pack, or incite them to rage, does the spirit need to temporarily eject from the host or just claim it if possible? In other words, how does a fettered spirit affect anything outside the host with influences?</div> </div> </div> </div>Loving the book, too.<br /> <br /> Core, p190. 'Most possessing spirits Fetter themselves to their intended hosts and use the Possess Manifestation Effect to take full control only in emergencies.' And while they can't use Influences or Numina on other targets while Fettering, you can use Influences on the one you're Fettered to (and it's cheaper).<br /> <br /> I think Broken Mirror would mostly just remain Fettered to Rebecca, and Urge her when something necessary came up, like to steer her into or away from some supernatural mischief. Then like it says 'When Broken Mirror desires more direct control, she uses the Possession Manifestation on Rebecca.'","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}